.TH GPAPERCTL 1 2026-11-27 "gpaperd 0.1.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
gpaperctl \- control a running gpaperd
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gpaperctl
.RB ( next | previous | ban | favorite | pause | resume )
.RB [ \-\-style
.IR STYLE ]
.br
.B gpaperctl set
.RB [ \-\-style
.IR STYLE ]
.I IMAGE
.br
.B gpaperctl unban
.I ID
.br
.B gpaperctl
.RB ( reload | refresh | restore )
.br
.B gpaperctl status
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B gpaperctl
sends one command to
.BR gpaperd (1)
over the session bus, at the name and interface
.BR io.github.worxbend.Gpaperd1 ,
object
.BR /io/github/worxbend/Gpaperd1 ,
and waits for the answer.
.B set
calls the method
.BR Set(style,\ id) ,
whose
.I id
is an absolute, canonical path or an
.B http
or
.B https
URL.
.BR ban ,
.B unban
and
.B favorite
call
.BR Ban(style) ,
.B Unban(id)
and
.BR Favorite(style) .
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B next
Rotate now.
.TP
.B previous
Show the previous image again.
Each style remembers the last 20 images it showed.
.TP
.BI set " IMAGE"
Show
.I IMAGE
now, as
.B next
shows the image it picks: the interval starts again, the image it
replaces goes into the history, so
.B previous
returns to it, and a pause stays as it is.
.I IMAGE
is a local file, made absolute and canonical against the current
directory, or a remote URL as the config lists it.
It must be in the sources of each style meant; otherwise the command fails
with
.B org.freedesktop.DBus.Error.InvalidArgs
and nothing changes.
It also fails while the style's sources are still being scanned, when a
remote image is not downloaded yet, and when the image fails its check.
When the image fails its check or cannot be written, the image on screen
stays and its interval starts again.
Setting the image already on screen only starts the interval again.
.TP
.B ban
Ban the image on screen in each style meant, then rotate each one as
.B next
does.
A banned image is never shown again in either style: no rotation,
.BR next ,
.B previous
or
.B set
picks it, until
.BR unban .
The ban is saved and survives a restart.
No file is deleted or moved.
A style left without another image follows
.BR empty_style :
it shows the other style's image, or with
.B keep\-current
keeps the banned image on screen, and the command fails while the ban
stays.
A style that shows nothing, whose background key is missing or locked,
or that is paused by an outside key change or by
.BR restore ,
fails and bans nothing.
A
.B pause
does not stop a ban.
.TP
.BI unban " ID"
Lift the ban of
.IR ID ,
the path or URL as
.B status
lists it.
A URL with credentials or a query string must be typed as the config
lists it, since
.B status
does not print those parts.
The image is in rotation again, as a new file is.
An
.I ID
that is not banned fails with
.BR org.freedesktop.DBus.Error.InvalidArgs .
.TP
.B favorite
Copy the image on screen in each style meant into
.B favorites_dir
of the config, which is created when missing.
The copy keeps the image's file name; a remote image is named after the
last path segment of its URL.
A file that is there already is never replaced: the copy gets a numeric
suffix, such as
.IR day\-1.jpg .
Fails when the config sets no
.BR favorites_dir ,
when a style meant shows nothing or is paused by an outside key change or
by
.BR restore ,
and with the I/O error when a copy cannot be written.
.TP
.B pause
Stop the timer of a style.
The pause is saved and survives a restart of the daemon.
.TP
.B resume
End a pause by
.B gpaperctl
and a pause that an external key change caused; that key is written back.
A style whose change is overdue rotates at once; any other keeps its
deadline.
.TP
.B reload
Read the config file again and apply it.
An invalid file is refused with its line and column, and the running config
stays.
.TP
.B refresh
Revalidate every remote image now.
.TP
.B restore
Write back the background keys the user had before
.B gpaperd
first wrote them, and pause both styles.
.B resume
hands the keys back to
.BR gpaperd .
A key that an administrator locked stays as it is: every other key is
written back, and the command fails naming the locked keys.
Fails when no original keys are saved.
After the state file is lost, keys that name a slot or a downloaded image
are not saved as originals.
With
.BR "apply_mode = \(dquri\(dq" ,
a key that names a local image is saved as an original then, and
.B restore
writes that image back.
.TP
.B status
Print the style on screen, the next change in local time, and for each
style the image in its slot, its catalog size, its usable and bad images,
and why it is paused, then the banned images.
A remote image is shown by its URL without credentials and without the
query string.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-style " STYLE"
The style a command acts on:
.BR light ,
.BR dark ,
.B visible
(the style on screen, the default) or
.BR both .
.TP
.B \-\-json
.RB ( status )
Print the daemon's JSON document as it is sent:
.BR version ,
.BR visible ,
.B next_change
(Unix seconds or null), and per style
.BR current ,
.BR paused ,
.BR items ,
.B usable
and
.BR bad ,
then
.BR banned ,
the list of banned ids.
Remote ids are printed without credentials, query string or fragment.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The daemon carried out the command.
.TP
.B 1
The daemon is not running or did not answer, the session bus cannot be
reached, the reload was refused, the image of
.B set
cannot be found, or the daemon reported an error: for example a
.B favorite
without
.BR favorites_dir .
With
.BR "apply_mode = \(dquri\(dq" ,
.BR next ,
.B previous
and
.B set
also exit 1 when the image changed but the key write waits for a retry
after a failed write, or for the 1 second wait of
.BR "on_external_change = \(dqreassert\-now\(dq" .
The reason goes to stderr.
.TP
.B 2
A usage error, such as an unknown command or style.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.EX
gpaperctl next \-\-style both
gpaperctl pause \-\-style dark
gpaperctl set \-\-style both ~/Pictures/Wallpapers/lake.jpg
gpaperctl ban
gpaperctl unban /home/me/Pictures/Wallpapers/grey.jpg
gpaperctl favorite \-\-style both
gpaperctl status
gpaperctl status \-\-json | jq .styles.light.current
.EE
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR gpaperd (1),
.BR gpaperd.toml (5),
.BR busctl (1)
